WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.710
Welcome to Mixiuh News,

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:02.875
our new breaking AI

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:03.650
news section.

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.610
Just fourteen days after launching

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.560
Gemini four Argon for fast

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:08.660
everyday tasks,

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:09.545
Google DeepMind has

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:10.585
unveiled its bigger

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:12.455
brother: Gemini four Carbon.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:15.140
Rather than replacing Argon,

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:17.405
Carbon is Google's heavy-duty

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:18.900
reasoning flagship,

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:20.485
debuting today at number

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.735
one worldwide on the

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:22.785
Artificial Analysis

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:23.870
Index with fifty-nine

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.555
points, ahead of Claude

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:26.835
Opus five point five

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.670
and GPT-six Astra.

00:00:29.045 --> 00:00:30.020
What does that mean

00:00:30.025 --> 00:00:30.805
in practice?

00:00:30.965 --> 00:00:32.390
Imagine handing an AI

00:00:32.395 --> 00:00:33.140
a massive

00:00:33.145 --> 00:00:33.860
ten-thousand-file

00:00:33.865 --> 00:00:35.170
repository with a deep

00:00:35.175 --> 00:00:36.000
kernel bug.

00:00:36.005 --> 00:00:37.210
While standard models

00:00:37.215 --> 00:00:37.775
lose track

00:00:38.045 --> 00:00:38.960
after a few minutes,

00:00:38.965 --> 00:00:39.920
Google's engineers

00:00:39.925 --> 00:00:41.000
watched Carbon work

00:00:41.005 --> 00:00:42.420
continuously for days

00:00:42.425 --> 00:00:43.680
until it isolated the

00:00:43.685 --> 00:00:44.485
root cause.

00:00:44.645 --> 00:00:45.700
That is why it

00:00:45.705 --> 00:00:46.697
hits nine point six

00:00:46.702 --> 00:00:48.025
percent on SWE-sweep,

00:00:48.345 --> 00:00:49.640
more than double Argon

00:00:49.645 --> 00:00:50.245
and nearly

00:00:50.425 --> 00:00:51.360
triple Opus,

00:00:51.365 --> 00:00:52.300
while retaining

00:00:52.305 --> 00:00:53.135
ninety-six point two percent

00:00:53.405 --> 00:00:54.430
accuracy across one

00:00:54.435 --> 00:00:55.475
million tokens.

00:00:55.775 --> 00:00:56.930
Its biggest breakthrough

00:00:56.935 --> 00:00:58.715
is practical cybersecurity.

00:00:59.545 --> 00:01:00.805
On SEC-bench Pro,

00:01:01.045 --> 00:01:01.720
the model isn't

00:01:01.725 --> 00:01:02.775
answering multiple-choice

00:01:03.015 --> 00:01:04.230
trivia, it audits real

00:01:04.235 --> 00:01:05.410
production codebases to

00:01:05.415 --> 00:01:06.485
uncover hidden vulnerabilities

00:01:06.735 --> 00:01:07.420
on its own,

00:01:07.575 --> 00:01:08.356
setting an eighty-eight

00:01:08.361 --> 00:01:08.995
point two percent

00:01:09.105 --> 00:01:10.500
record versus sixty-two

00:01:10.505 --> 00:01:11.325
point eight percent

00:01:11.445 --> 00:01:12.715
for DeepSeek four point

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:13.445
one Flash.

00:01:14.105 --> 00:01:16.030
Then on ExploitGym,

00:01:16.035 --> 00:01:17.325
it spins up a sandbox

00:01:17.595 --> 00:01:18.970
and builds a working

00:01:18.975 --> 00:01:20.400
proof-of-concept exploit

00:01:20.405 --> 00:01:22.125
fifty-four point eight percent

00:01:22.375 --> 00:01:23.100
of the time to

00:01:23.105 --> 00:01:24.605
prove the bug is real.

00:01:25.235 --> 00:01:26.410
Once a bug is found,

00:01:26.415 --> 00:01:27.350
you have to patch

00:01:27.355 --> 00:01:28.375
it without breaking the app.

00:01:29.275 --> 00:01:31.535
That is what CWE-bench measures:

00:01:31.955 --> 00:01:32.740
running directly as an

00:01:32.745 --> 00:01:34.755
agent inside Google Antigravity,

00:01:35.335 --> 00:01:36.040
Carbon patches

00:01:36.045 --> 00:01:36.780
seventy-one percent

00:01:36.785 --> 00:01:38.625
of root-cause vulnerabilities,

00:01:39.475 --> 00:01:40.900
beating Grok four point seven,

00:01:40.905 --> 00:01:43.495
GPT-six Astra on Codex,

00:01:43.735 --> 00:01:44.830
and Claude Opus on

00:01:44.835 --> 00:01:45.925
Claude Code.

00:01:46.735 --> 00:01:46.810
In fact,

00:01:46.815 --> 00:01:48.240
Google's own Chrome

00:01:48.245 --> 00:01:49.760
security team reported

00:01:49.765 --> 00:01:51.080
Carbon performed over

00:01:51.085 --> 00:01:52.400
ten times better than

00:01:52.405 --> 00:01:53.640
a rival lab's frontier

00:01:53.645 --> 00:01:54.860
model at generating real

00:01:54.865 --> 00:01:55.465
browser patches.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:57.145
What if an

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.735
attacker tries to hijack

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:00.030
the AI agent itself?

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:01.955
On Gray Swan's indirect

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:03.260
prompt injection benchmark,

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:04.755
malicious instructions

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.039
are hidden inside web

00:02:06.044 --> 00:02:07.485
pages or documents to

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:08.475
trick the agent into

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:09.600
leaking your keys.

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:10.770
While GPT-six

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.135
Astra falls for the

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:13.008
trap eight point five

00:02:13.013 --> 00:02:13.810
percent of the

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:14.230
time,

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:15.570
Carbon blocked one

00:02:15.575 --> 00:02:16.375
hundred percent of

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:17.557
attacks with a zero

00:02:17.562 --> 00:02:18.165
point zero percent

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:18.875
breach rate,

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:19.430
while dropping

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:20.735
Terminal-Bench cheating

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.555
to zero and cutting hallucinations

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:22.910
in half.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:24.525
To test real-world

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:25.820
long-term planning,

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:27.650
Vending-Bench two puts

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.515
the AI in charge

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:30.675
of a simulated vending

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:31.610
machine company,

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:34.200
managing inventory, suppliers,

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:35.335
dynamic pricing,

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:36.105
and cash flow

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:37.595
without going broke.

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:39.175
Carbon finishes with

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:39.879
sixteen thousand four

00:02:39.884 --> 00:02:40.546
hundred eighty-four

00:02:40.551 --> 00:02:41.810
dollars in the bank,

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:42.395
seventy-eight percent

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.295
more profit than Claude

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.695
Opus five point five's

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:46.306
nine thousand two

00:02:46.311 --> 00:02:47.039
hundred thirty-five

00:02:47.044 --> 00:02:48.095
dollars, while also

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.685
leading advanced math at

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:50.365
eighty percent on

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:51.505
RiemannBench and

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:53.180
computer use at seventy-seven

00:02:53.511 --> 00:02:53.930
point four percent.

00:02:54.635 --> 00:02:55.465
When can you use it

00:02:55.635 --> 00:02:56.290
and what does it

00:02:56.295 --> 00:02:56.985
really cost?

00:02:57.135 --> 00:02:58.490
Today Carbon rolls out

00:02:58.495 --> 00:02:59.570
in early access to

00:02:59.575 --> 00:03:00.790
vetted cyber defenders

00:03:00.795 --> 00:03:02.130
and institutions through

00:03:02.135 --> 00:03:02.920
Google's Fairwind

00:03:02.925 --> 00:03:03.830
initiative before

00:03:03.835 --> 00:03:04.700
opening to all

00:03:04.805 --> 00:03:06.130
developers in AI Studio,

00:03:06.135 --> 00:03:07.710
Vertex AI,

00:03:07.715 --> 00:03:08.655
and Antigravity.

00:03:08.975 --> 00:03:09.940
And watch the fine

00:03:09.945 --> 00:03:10.890
print in Google's

00:03:10.895 --> 00:03:11.705
official blog:

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:12.860
while it launches at

00:03:12.865 --> 00:03:14.210
Argon's promo rate of

00:03:14.215 --> 00:03:15.250
two and ten dollars

00:03:15.255 --> 00:03:16.475
per million tokens,

00:03:16.915 --> 00:03:18.030
after the introductory

00:03:18.035 --> 00:03:19.230
period it doubles to

00:03:19.235 --> 00:03:19.970
four dollars input and

00:03:19.975 --> 00:03:20.835
twenty dollars output.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.205
So what do we

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:24.330
expect from Gemini four Carbon?

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.070
Remember that in our lab,

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:27.215
its smaller brother

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:28.605
Argon, with fifty

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:29.845
points, already beat

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:31.114
Claude Opus five point

00:03:31.119 --> 00:03:31.970
five four to two.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:33.805
With Carbon jumping to

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:35.135
fifty-nine points,

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:35.850
doubling agentic

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:36.580
coding,

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:37.585
and ranking fourth

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:39.300
worldwide on WebDev Arena,

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:40.665
we expect a massive

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:42.500
leap in three-D physics shaders,

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:43.785
live security patching,

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.190
and full multi-file apps.

